posts.text:
Nigerians, please come to my aid! repost if you come across this  .                                                                      

@theravenpay, also known as Raven Bank, has left me unable to access my funds, amounting to over ₦17 million.

After @Aprokodoctor publicly encouraged people to invest with Raven, which I did, now that i decided to liquidate my fixed deposit with the Raven bank. That was when my ordeal began.

I have been unable to withdraw my money. Initially, every transfer attempt returned the error: “Transfer failed, please try again later.” Then for months they claimed to be doing maintenance. Now, the app says I have “no spendable balance.”

I have also been trying to get a meeting with Raven Bank’s CEO, Uchenna Nnodim, but my scheduled meetings keep getting postponed from one month  to another.

@Aprokodoctor, you made a video encouraging people to invest with this bank. I am asking you to help amplify my complaint and get answers.

All I want is access to my money. Over ₦17 million is at stake, and I cannot afford to lose it. Even if Raven claims to have no money, atleast let them release part of the money to me.

Nigerians, please exercise caution before entrusting your money to any financial institution. If this can happen to me, it could happen to anyone.

@theravenpay, I need answers, and I need access to my funds.

More than six weeks without a single donation... Don't forget us, we need your support. Even a small donation makes a differenc 😔
